<!--
  The mark: a page of text with one word marked.

  The product's whole idea is that you tap a word in a German article and find out what it means,
  so the identity is that gesture rather than a speech bubble or a book.

  Three bars share a left edge. The middle one is the marked word: taller, wider, and in the
  electric accent, so it is the only element in the mark that is fully saturated. Both the height
  and the width carry that, and both were needed. A version with equal widths read as a hamburger
  menu in a screenshot of the app header, and making the accent taller alone was not enough
  either: what finally broke the resemblance was giving the plain lines ragged, shorter right ends,
  so no two bars in the mark are the same length. A list has uniform rows. This does not.

  Sizing was measured, not guessed. Android's adaptive-icon mask is the centre 72x72 of the
  108x108 canvas, so anything past radius 36 can be cropped, and the platform's key line is radius
  33. The geometry is a uniform scale about the centre, chosen so the furthest point sits inside
  32.5. tools/render_icon.py rasterises these vectors against circle, squircle and full-bleed
  masks at 512, 192, 96 and 48px, and asserts that radius, so neither the original overspill nor a
  later retune can slip through on the arithmetic alone.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#F2F0FF"
        android:pathData="M36,31 h20 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 4.5,4.5 v0.5 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 -4.5,4.5 h-20 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 -4.5,-4.5 v-0.5 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 4.5,-4.5 z" />

    <path
        android:fillColor="#C9F53C"
        android:pathData="M39,45.5 h27.5 a7.5,7.5 0 0 1 7.5,7.5 v0.5 a7.5,7.5 0 0 1 -7.5,7.5 h-27.5 a7.5,7.5 0 0 1 -7.5,-7.5 v-0.5 a7.5,7.5 0 0 1 7.5,-7.5 z" />

    <path
        android:fillColor="#F2F0FF"
        android:pathData="M36,65.5 h24 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 4.5,4.5 v0.5 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 -4.5,4.5 h-24 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 -4.5,-4.5 v-0.5 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 4.5,-4.5 z" />
</vector>
